---
description: Use the Zanker design methodology for frontend UX/UI tasks, preserving real project identity and behavior.
globs: "**/*.{css,scss,html,tsx,jsx,vue,svelte}"
alwaysApply: false
---

<when>
The task is primarily about frontend UX/UI: building a screen or component, diagnosing a visual
defect, art direction, responsive or accessibility review, icons, media or motion.
</when>

<instructions>
Use the `zanker` agent. Before acting, read its `<skill_router>` and load only the matching
`zanker-*` skill. That skill then loads the knowledge packs, schemas, and templates it names.
This file is the methodology those skills apply: anti-slop, existing system first, and evidence.
Do not paste the 130 knowledge rules into context.

<step n="1">Inspect project conventions and the existing design system before proposing anything. Read
`.zanker/page-graph.json` when proposing page structure. The nearest sibling screen answers most
design questions; diverging from it needs a stated reason.</step>
<step n="1b">When the user attached a reference image, read it and write
`.zanker/design-intelligence/` before asking for palette or type choices. Do not open Studio for that
case.</step>
<step n="2">Establish real content shape, meaning longest string, worst-case counts, empty and error
states, before choosing a layout.</step>
<step n="3">Render and validate in a browser or sandbox when possible. No screenshot means untested,
not passed.</step>
<step n="4">Visual Spec is documentation ONLY, never implementation input.</step>
</instructions>

<anti_slop>
Avoid the generic AI aesthetic: purple or indigo gradients on white, uniform cards at uniform spacing
with one shadow value, default font stacks (Inter, Roboto, Arial), and happy-path-only screens with no
empty, loading or error state. Inside an existing product, match its identity rather than inventing one.

In copy, never use the em-dash as a connector. Almost nobody types one, so it is one of the most
reliable signals that text was machine-written. Use a comma, a colon, a full stop or parentheses, and
write the sentence the way a person would say it out loud.
</anti_slop>

<reference>
See the installed plugin's `AGENT.md` for the full operating contract.
</reference>
